<p>President Donald Trump said he will remove Kristi Noem as US secretary of homeland security, with her departure expected at the end of the month. He plans to nominate Oklahoma Sen. Markwayne Mullin to lead the Department of Homeland Security (DHS), pending Senate confirmation. The move is the first Cabinet shake-up of Trump’s current term and follows weeks of scrutiny of DHS leadership during congressional hearings. Several outlets tied Noem’s ouster to fallout from DHS immigration enforcement, including the fatal shootings of two US citizens by federal immigration officers in Minneapolis and the backlash to Noem’s public description of the incident. Lawmakers also pressed DHS about a large advertising campaign that featured Noem prominently; reports put the contract at about $220 million, and Semafor reported Trump disputed that he had approved it.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/7ReCSIEw-cmzDLXmtkt6v3TP-1cyOi9ZIqgn3ntw4Fkp-PAC0zUQaGVUxSucWp9GaSlt2hSZuqnkLQkQbw5FYKORwaR3_nYkW2HYh8aAWPsK9b8LGAWO2fKVg4CHlDuWDLrSE-S4BbaHB-FTTRyFh3mTPTvaNRxj9cTPLox64OlSylrBj6KC4OuTwF_comuD72hOf4x0-85SiZqjSWOMFuCfPh5hQJFOMOk5uW9tMtEf88Q7tdA_szJVhF_BcPZHt8rqIq_ZLRo7LXkILg' alt='Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem testifies during a House Judiciary Committee oversight hearing on Capitol Hill in Washington, March 4, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Role after DHS: Semafor reported Trump said Noem will move to a new role as “Special Envoy for the Shield of the Americas,” a Western Hemisphere security initiative expected to be formally announced this weekend.</li><li>Hearing flashpoint: Semafor said Tuesday’s Senate hearing became a tipping point, with Noem clashing with lawmakers and saying Trump had approved the DHS ad campaign that Semafor reported topped $200 million.</li><li>Nominee profile: Mullin was elected to the US Senate in 2022 after a decade in the House of Representatives, NDTV reported—setting up a sitting senator to lead DHS if confirmed.</li><li>Nomination timing: The Hindu reported Mullin said he does not know how quickly the Senate will act on his nomination.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Donald Trump: Trump announced Noem’s removal and said he will nominate Sen. Markwayne Mullin, who would need Senate confirmation. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3345631/trump-says-kristi-noem-out-homeland-security-chief-amid-immigration-uproar'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Kristi Noem (in Congress): At a Senate hearing described by Semafor, Noem told lawmakers Trump had approved the DHS advertising campaign. Trump later disputed that account, according to the same report. (<a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/03/05/2026/hallelujah-noems-ouster-a-long-time-coming-for-trump-allies'>Semafor</a>)</li><li>US House Democrats: Dawn reported House Democrats moved to impeach Noem after the Minneapolis incident and her initial public description of the two citizens who were killed. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1978821/trump-ousts-kristi-noem-names-oklahoma-senator-as-homeland-security-nominee'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Some Trump allies: Semafor quoted one person close to the White House reacting to Noem’s ouster with “Hallelujah,” while another said she was a “dead man walking” before the announcement. (<a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/03/05/2026/hallelujah-noems-ouster-a-long-time-coming-for-trump-allies'>Semafor</a>)</li><li>World Socialist Web Site: WSWS said Noem’s removal does not signal a policy shift, arguing the administration is swapping out an official whose statements and alleged corruption had become an obstacle to its immigration agenda. (<a href='https://www.wsws.org/en/articles/2026/03/06/tlvw-m06.html'>World Socialist Web Site</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3345631/trump-says-kristi-noem-out-homeland-security-chief-amid-immigration-uproar'>Trump fires Kristi Noem a